      "body": "### Preflight Checklist\n\n- [x] I have read the [Contributing Guidelines](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md) for this project.\n- [x] I agree to follow the [Code of Conduct](https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) that this project adheres to.\n- [x] I have searched the [issue tracker](https://www.github.com/electron/electron/issues) for a bug report that matches the one I want to file, without success.\n\n### Electron Version\n\n44.4.3 / 45.0.0-alpha.12 / 46.0.0-nightly.20260925\n\n### What operating system(s) are you using?\n\nmacOS\n\n### Operating System Version\n\nMacOS 27 (latest)\n\n### What arch are you using?\n\narm64 (including Apple Silicon)\n\n### Last Known Working Electron version\n\nN/A\n\n### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?\n\nYes\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nElectron starts successfully even if registration for system sleep/wake\nnotifications fails. That failure should degrade the unavailable notification\nfunctionality, not terminate the application or prevent independent battery\nand thermal monitors from initializing.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nElectron exits with a native SIGSEGV during startup, before application\nJavaScript runs. Application-level error handlers and logging therefore cannot\ncapture the failure.\n\nThe crash is in IOKit!IONotificationPortGetRunLoopSource, with\nEXC_BAD_ACCESS at address 0x10 on the main thread. It also occurs when\nlaunching fresh alpha/nightly Electron binaries with an isolated user-data\ndirectory and only --version, without loading the application's JavaScript.\n\n### Testcase Gist URL\n\nhttps://gist.github.com/mbianchidev/1fba9b144ba1c6bbb1393a2b1554dfd7\n\n### Additional Information\n\nChromium landed the fix on 2026-09-17:\n\nChromium issue: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/562777834\nReview: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8424840\nCommit: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/69403d85b78bef2370cc9f8206dce84c5ff63ea4\n\nI found a terrible workaround for two different projects but it's really AI slop so I would not submit it as a proper fix.",
